    "created_at": "2022-10-04T06:50:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-04T06:50:16Z",
    "body": "The most impactful remaining work is properly using the fetch hooks. Probably at the same time we would take care of the the processResponseConsumeBody and processCustomFetchResponse mismatch.\r\n\r\nRight now we _say_ we are using processResponseConsumeBody, but we are really using it more like processResponse plus magically treating the body as if it were a byte sequence. https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-elsewhere outlines the proper usage. Basically:\r\n\r\n- Change the signature from (response) to (response, bodyBytes)\r\n- Insert bail-outs when bodyBytes is null or failure. Probably this can replace existing bailouts for response being a network error / response's type being \"error\".\r\n- Replace operations on the response's body with operations on bodyBytes.\r\n- Update processCustomFetchResponse to have the same signature and, for its implementations, behavior\r\n- Update worklet module response maps to be (response, bodyBytes) tuples, probably.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
